# Line endings are LF everywhere: in the repository and in the working tree,
# Windows checkouts included. Git, node, python and the shell tools all write
# LF, so a CRLF working tree meant every one-line edit came back as a
# whole-file diff, `grep 'foo$'` quietly matched nothing, and build.sh carried
# a stray \r into the end of every variable it set.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The tsum portrait library is generated, compared byte for byte by the tool
# that writes it, and copied verbatim into dist/ and onto the device. A CRLF
# checkout on Windows would make that comparison fail on a clean clone and grow
# every line by a byte on the way to the phone, so it stays LF everywhere.
*.dat text eol=lf

# Binary: never end-of-line converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary

# Documentation media. Same rule as the images above.
*.mp4 binary
*.webp binary
*.mkv binary
